sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-conus-second-assessor-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Quantitative metrics are genuinely computed on the output and compared to specimen numbers: H/W 1.8342 vs 1.8330, silhouette IoU 0.835, white-chord mean/CV, KS of mean-normalised chords, pigment fraction and a box-counting dimension, all written to CSV and drawn in panel F; the Rule 30 geometric law P(W=w)=2^-w (mean 2, CV 0.707) is correctly derived and confirmed. Deductions: the chord metric has no discriminating power, since Rule 90 (KS 0.2627, CV 0.697) and Rule 150 (KS 0.252) match Rule 30 (KS 0.2623, CV 0.7075) and Rule 110 scores better (KS 0.2448), and the specimen CV 0.640 is actually closer to the Rule 90 control; this is never stated (deduction 20). The box-counting estimator returns 2.155 for iid random bits and 2.17 for Rule 30, which is impossible for a planar set, so D_box is invalid (deduction 10). H/W and IoU are calibration, not validation: the mesh constants were tuned to the same single outline the self-test then asserts within 1.5 percent (deduction 10). The specimen-derived numbers are not reproducible (no segmentation code; the 1814 chord runs cannot be regenerated from the vendored 148x92 lattice, which yields 667 runs of mean 11.5), only one of two specimens is used quantitatively, and the Meinhardt CV test window 0.60-1.35 is nearly vacuous (deduction 15). Evidence: 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L836–L854: H/W, IoU, KS and box-dimension comparisons against fixture values; thresholds 1.5 percent and IoU>0.82 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L836-L854>; conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): Rule 30 KS 0.2623 vs Rule 90 KS 0.2627; D_box 2.17 and 2.15 exceed 2; pigment fraction 0.50 vs specimen 0.355 — conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, text/csv, 644 B, artifact_sha256 da34a299061268e937c073cc835a76f836bf1d976c145e9484147e922e21fa19 (sha256 da34a299061268e937c073cc835a76f836bf1d976c145e9484147e922e21fa19), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L740–L753: box_counting_dimension on edges with scales 2..32 of a 148x92 grid; gives 2.155 on iid noise <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L740-L753>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L829–L834: Meinhardt tent test accepts any CV in [0.60, 1.35]; current value 1.1045 while README reports 0.6929 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L829-L834>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): Rule 30 center-column exact match to OEIS A051023 (first 128 bits) = 128 bits matched (reference 128, Wolfram 1984 Nature 311:419 / OEIS A051023 / Rule 30 Prize (2019)) [exact bitwise comparison of a_{t,0} (t=0..127) against OEIS A051023]; Jen (1990) left-bijective inverse & diagonal recursion bit errors = 0 bit errors (reference 0, Jen 1990 Physica D 45:3-18 Theorem 1 & Section 2) [sum of bit reconstruction errors across a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) and d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t))] — first 5 period-doubling dislocation diagonals k = [0, 3, 8, 29, 400] (P = 1, 2, 4, 8, 16); Rule 30 Prize #2 center-column density c_1024 = 0.4785 fraction of 1s (reference 0.5, Wolfram 2019 Rule 30 Prize Problem 2 (https://rule30prize.org/)) [cumulative fraction (1/N) sum_{t=0}^{1023} a_{t,0} on single-seed light-cone] — normalized 4-bit block Shannon entropy H_4/4 = 0.99640 bits/bit; left-cone periodic crystal lock-in front velocity v_lock = -0.1962 cells/step (reference -0.2081, Jen 1990 Physica D 45:3-18 / Wolfram 2002 A New Kind of Science p. 871) [spatial drift velocity of period-locked diagonal boundary (1/slope - 1 from T_lock(k) = 1.2441*k + 7.89 over k in [30, 400])] — damage-cone velocities: v_R = +1.0000±0.0000, v_L = -0.2604±0.1024 cells/step; 3D Raup Conus textile shell height-to-width ratio (H/W) = 1.8342 ratio (H/W) (reference 1.833, Conus textile OSU specimen 24399204286 (James St. John, CC BY 2.0)) [projected axial height / maximum shoulder diameter of 3D Raup Conus mesh (W=1.42, D=0.05, T=3.15)]; 2D shell silhouette IoU vs segmented Conus textile specimen = 0.8353 IoU (intersection/union) (reference 1.0, Conus textile OSU specimen 24399204286 (datasets/conus/conus_textile_specimen.jpg)) [pixel overlap between projected 3D Raup Conus mesh and segmented OSU Conus textile specimen silhouette (256x140 grid)]; Rule 30 white-tent chord-length CV (σ/μ) = 0.7075 CV (std/mean) (reference 0.6403, Conus textile OSU specimen dorsal white-tent segmentation (1,814 chords, CV=0.6403; exact geometric P(W=w)=2^{-w} theory CV=0.7071)) [coefficient of variation of horizontal unpigmented run lengths w on periodic mantle ring (230x370)] — Meinhardt-Klingler PDE CV = 1.1045 (vs close-up specimen ling_commons_010 CV = 1.1310); KS(Rule30, specimen) = 0.2623." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.45"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-morphometric-validation> rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation (1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py, docs/media/conus_textile_rule30.gif, docs/media/conus_rule30_kymograph_defect_fronts.png, conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv, conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphometric validation' for Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail)" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

